{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1386270-hermetic-chantry-in-horizon-realm-ideas-for-servants","id":1386270,"title":"Hermetic Chantry in Horizon Realm: Ideas for Servants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-06T22:58:56-07:00","id":1386270,"title":"Hermetic Chantry in Horizon Realm: Ideas for Servants","content":"Hello. I'm designing a Hermetic chantry for my chronicle, based on a very simple Horizon Realm. I started working on this earlier today, basically from scratch. I tried to keep the &quot;hermetic vibe&quot; with symbolism everywhere.<br /> <br /> Berore I ask my question, I'll give you the whole context.<br /> <br /> <b>Name</b>: University of Saint Nichodemus<br /> <br /> <b>Short History</b>: 3 masters who studied under the famous Archmage Nichodemus decided it was time to pass the teachings of their mentor to future generations 20 years before the starting time of the chronicle. They triumvirate decided to establish the place outside Earth to not be entirely bound by consensus and world-related.<br /> <br /> <b>Goals</b>: 1. initiate recently awakened mages into the Hermetic Tradition<br /> 2. Providing shelter for &quot;older&quot; hermetic mages in case of need<br /> 3. Be used as base of operations for the university's founders.<br /> <br /> <b>Students</b>: Between 20 and 25 awakened from different countries all around the Americas.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization</b>: The University is divided in 3 different Colleges; each one represented by a moment of the day, a primary color, and a Word.<br /> <br /> 1. The &quot;<b>Morning College</b>&quot; (<i><b>dark</b></i> <b><i>yellow</i></b>) trains recruits to interact with the mortal world through the Hermetic paradigm. Day improves its students social, investigative and bureaucratic skills. It trains them to gather human and material resources to sustain and expand the Order's influence on the Sleeping world.<br /> WORD: <b>COLLECT</b>. Spheres taught there: <b>Mind</b>, <b>Entropy</b>, <b>Time</b>.<br /> <br /> 2. The &quot;<b>Twilight College</b>&quot; (<i><b>dark</b></i> <i><b>red</b></i>) teach students the corpus of main Hermetic practices: alchemy, occult, history, languages, medicine, high ritual, magical theory, etc Twilight improves its students mental skills and knowledge, cultivating their divine potential. WORD: <b>BUILD</b>. Spheres taught there: <b>Matter</b>, <b>Spirit</b>, <b>Prime</b>.<br /> <br /> 3. The &quot;<b>Night College</b>&quot; (<i><b>dark blue</b></i>) shape students for physical, mental and magical struggle. Night train them in different types of combat, resistance, meditation and survival techniques, anatomy and medicine, battle tactics, etc. Night is a factory of soldiers for the Ascension War. WORD: <b>PROTECT</b>. Spheres taught; <b>Forces</b>, <b>Life</b>, <b>Correspondence</b>.<br /> <br /> Students are tested by each master and sent to a primary college. As their education moves forward, they can take courses in the other colleges.<br /> <br /> Each Master is the head of one College and its main teacher. They are the Seat of Morning, the Seat of Twilight and the Seat of Night. They make all decisions regarding Saint Nichodemus as a Triumvirate.<br /> <br /> <b>Physical Space</b>: The 3 Colleges are located in the same building. From the air, the facilities look like an equilateral triangle, each side built as a hall of 2 floors with a Tower (the Seat's individual chambers) in the exact center. The first floor is for classrooms and laboratories, while the second is for students living spaces (bedrooms, livingrooms and restrooms). The Halls and Towers show different architechture. Each one belongs to a College and it's painted with its color (inside and outside), mixed with some white.<br /> The triangle vertexes are doors leading to earthbound locations controlled by the Order. When you arrive to the campus from either entrance, you are in the &quot;angles&quot; of the triangle: connection points between the 3 Halls. They're grey areas - neutral ground - not painted with any of the colors. The yard lies on the &quot;inside&quot; of the triangle, following a straight line from the entrances. .<br /> The &quot;inside&quot; of the triangle is the yard: a peaceful green lawn whose center holds 3 sculptures of the same man, each one facing one of the doors, welcoming students and visitors alike: Nichodemus himself, in a &quot;Trimegistus&quot; arrangement.<br /> The University (the triangle) is protected by an invisible dome of Quintessence. Through the dome, it's possible to see a recreation of a normal, clear sky. The doors, as mentioned before, connect with Earth. If someone manages to go through the Hall's outermost walls or the dome, that person would be floating in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Now, the question. Clearly, a place like the one I just described must have SOMEONE in charge of the upkeeping (cleaning, cooking, etc) and, probably, security (just in case the mages need an extra hand), Thing is, I dont want Sleepers working there.<br /> <br /> <b>What kind of magical servants could be working on the place?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","user":"Argonot","date":". 05-07-2020, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T00:52:59-07:00","id":1386634,"title":"","content":"That's a thought... Intelligent stone atomata? An army of animated items? A single, overworked, grumpy bound spirit or demon? One workaholic mage co-located all over the place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T14:07:36-07:00","id":1386776,"title":"","content":"Older Hermetic probably bring in some servants.<br /> <br /> With different shades of light, I would assume lots of spirits of light and color. Since you have functions of collecting, building and protecting, I would also see various elemental spirits.<br /> <br /> Taking some D&amp;D ideas from when I had a need to keep a dungeon clean, there would be something<br /> <br /> like<br /> <br /> 1. a gelatinous cube to clean up organic matter<br /> 2. something like a rust monster to get rid of all the metal lying around (in my dungeon, it was magnetic so it attracted metal to disarm and disarmor PCs)<br /> 3. a disenchanter (thing which touched magic items and destroyed them) to clean up magical things.<br /> <br /> Add in some spirits that build basic things as well as fire, earth, air and water elementals and some basic metal elements to reflect alchemical practices and you've got your spirits.<br /> <br /> A big chantry will have, in addition to apprentices, a few consors. I'd figure on some guards or instructors in mundane topics, human staff who can clean things that spirits that aren't too bright won't clean correctly, and of course, a librarian.<br /> <br /> Other life will be what is needed to sustain the chantry in the Horizon Realm plus whatever lifeforms seem cool. Bygones such as unicorns and dragons are worth having around. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T16:02:36-07:00","id":1387112,"title":"","content":"Homunculi servents.<br /> Combat Butlers.<br /> Bound spirits/jinn/elementals/etc.<br /> Talos-style bronze automatons.<br /> House elves (boggins?)<br /> Nephilim<br /> Sentient books.<br /> A Sphynx. <br /> <br /> Also the usual collection of mundane mortal grogs (house keepers, cooks, security guards, groundskeepers, clerks, etc.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}